{
  "title": "Pilot's own hand is redacted to a count on the board_unchanged path",
  "description": "On decisions where the bridge returns board_unchanged, the \
pilot is shown its own hand as a count instead of its cards, so it chooses an \
action without seeing what it holds. Measured on two real games: 8/73 and \
11/53 tool calls carry board_unchanged, i.e. 11-21% of decisions. \
Independently reconstructing the prompts through render_for_pilot showed the \
pilot rendered as '- You' with hand as a count in 8/70 and 10/50 decision \
prompts.\n\nMechanism: build_decision in src/magebench/pilot/pilot_bridge.py \
constructs Decision with player=\"You\" and only overwrites it from the board \
entry whose is_you is true. A board_unchanged result carries no board, so \
player stays the literal \"You\". render_player in \
src/magebench/game/decision_renderer.py then shows a full hand only when name \
== deciding_player, and no player is ever named \"You\", so the pilot's own \
hand is redacted along with the opponent's.\n\nThe fix is to carry the pilot's \
real username through the board_unchanged path rather than leaving the \"You\" \
placeholder — the same board_unchanged result already reaches a renderer that \
has the previous board, so the name is the only thing missing. Do not paper \
over it in the renderer by special-casing the string \"You\": that hides the \
same bug for any future caller that forgets to set the name.\n\nNote for \
whoever fixes this: it changes what the policy sees, so game results from \
before and after are not comparable. It likely warrants a HARNESS_EPOCH bump. \
Anything training on these games (GRPO rollouts) is currently learning from a \
reward that penalises decisions the harness made blind.\n\nAdd a test that a \
board_unchanged decision renders the deciding player's hand as cards, not as a \
count.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
